# What this module needs that no single spoon owns.
#
# Format is name | kind | locator | policy | reason, the same five fields a spoon uses. The
# collector stamps the consumer column with this module's name, since the need belongs to the
# module as a whole rather than to anything inside it.
#
# Nothing here is read by the running config. The resolver inside .hammerspoon serves spoons and
# probes only what a spoon declared, so a need like the application itself, which has no runtime
# consumer because nothing would be running without it, is declared here instead.
#
# Named dependencies-module rather than dependencies because this directory already holds the
# generated DEPENDENCIES, and on a case insensitive filesystem those two names are one file.
hammerspoon | app | org.hammerspoon.Hammerspoon | required | the application this entire module configures

# The seven core capabilities the composition root takes for itself rather than handing to a
# spoon it configures. Six are atoms that moved into Olm's lib in phase five of the olm build
# plan and retired for good once every other tool had passed its own validation, so the root
# assigns each straight to the spoon global of the same name and no second side is left to
# disagree with it. They belong here rather than beside a spoon because the taker is init.lua,
# which is the module as a whole rather than anything inside it, and it is the one file in this
# config that no spoon owns.
#
# registry joined in phase seven. The root builds its own instance from this factory rather
# than assigning the module straight to a global, and hands that instance to the launcher, but
# the reason for declaring it here is the same, init.lua is the sole taker and no plugin ever
# reaches for it.
#
# Required, all seven, because there is no degraded config without them. These lines only say
# that the root is handed these seven and that the files answering for them are where they are
# supposed to be.
panel | core | lib/panel.lua | required | the shared canvas surface behind every preview pane, docked hint bar, and cheat sheet
cheatsheet | core | lib/cheatsheet.lua | required | the shared overlay renderer both cheat sheets draw through
chordkey | core | lib/chordkey.lua | required | the shared hold and tap engine every leader key registers into
hyperkey | core | lib/hyperkey.lua | required | the leader modal every Hyper binding and every Hyper context binds into
chooser | core | lib/chooser/init.lua | required | the picker facade every list tool in this config is built on
deps | core | lib/deps.lua | required | the declaration reader that hands every other spoon its resolved tools
registry | core | lib/registry.lua | required | the tool registry the launcher's special row dispatch now asks first
